      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FULL NOISE (8) finds it hard to break through. Finished in the minors latest when second (29.67) at this track and may be close to breaking through. Makes plenty of appeal. DETECTION (3) ran below best last time finishing fourth (26.04) over 460m at Geelong from Box 6. Form from his last run is proving strong. Likely to play a prominent role. GREYSYND BONNIE (1) was prominent early from the tricky draw and did a fair job to be beaten 2.25 lengths into third (29.75) at this track in a Grade 5 over 515m. Is yet to miss the placings from this draw, including two wins, from four starts. Must be included in calculations. SIR TRENTON (4) is new to this course but not to be underestimated.",
